Date: Fri, 30 Jan 2026 23:31:43 +0000
Subject: Revert "memcg: use ratelimited stats flush in the reclaim"

This commit needs to be reverted for kernel 6.18 as it causes significant
MongoDB performance regressions on 4xlarge EC2 instances (c7g, c8g, c7a, c7i)
across both aarch64 and x86_64 architectures.

MongoDB benchmarks using YCSB show an average 12% regression compared to
kernel 6.12 baseline. Reverting this commit fully recovers performance with no
negative impact on other workloads.

The ratelimited stats flush optimization creates a bottleneck in the reclaim
path for MongoDB's memory access patterns on these instance sizes.

Signed-off-by: Shaoying Xu <shaoyi@amazon.com>

diff --git a/mm/vmscan.c b/mm/vmscan.c
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@ -2363,11 +2363,10 @@ static void prepare_scan_control(pg_data_t *pgdat, struct scan_control *sc)
 	target_lruvec = mem_cgroup_lruvec(sc->target_mem_cgroup, pgdat);
 
 	/*
-	 * Flush the memory cgroup stats in rate-limited way as we don't need
-	 * most accurate stats here. We may switch to regular stats flushing
-	 * in the future once it is cheap enough.
+	 * Flush the memory cgroup stats, so that we read accurate per-memcg
+	 * lruvec stats for heuristics.
 	 */
-	mem_cgroup_flush_stats_ratelimited(sc->target_mem_cgroup);
+	mem_cgroup_flush_stats(sc->target_mem_cgroup);
 
 	/*
 	 * Determine the scan balance between anon and file LRUs.
